sequenceDiagram
  %% Current flow: stage 3 of the command development pipeline. The author runs the designed proof in the task copy where the feature was built, using that copy's nested fleet. Every required case must pass before a PR opens. The command contract is docs/cli/proof/proof.mmd; copy proofs do not replay cases on the merge base.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 3 · end-to-end proof before PR
  %% kind: pipeline.3-proof
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=amber
  participant AG as Author<br/>Gateway access
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>verify workflow
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>candidate checkout
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>Gateway · 2 Nodes
  AG->>GW: Prove the command<br/>orbit proof COMMAND --group=GROUP
  %%> Command:
  %%> - orbit proof COMMAND --group=GROUP
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - call from a Node with Gateway access; the named group's active copy must keep its own nested fleet
  %%> - the proof uses the copy's current checkout, committed or not; no new copy is created
  Note over GW: Admit the proof<br/>group · copy · cases
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a missing group, an unavailable copy, a missing fleet or competing work; records intent without replay inputs
  GW->>SW: Start the run<br/>proof-fleet-verify
  SW->>CP: Plan the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - loads the cases from the copy's checkout before changing the fleet; invalid definitions fail the proof
  loop each batch in declared order
    SW->>CP: Reset the inner fleet<br/>restore base · apply · ready
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - resets before each batch, the first included; starts the containers and migrates the nested Gateway before readiness checks
    %%> - a failed reset stops the run; later cases are unrun with cause infrastructure
    SW->>CP: Run the batch<br/>setup · cases
    CP->>NT: Exercise and check<br/>real CLI · real effects
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the shared runner prepares the candidate prerequisites and callers, applies batch setup and checks each case's observable outcome
    %%> - cases use their own resources and undo nothing; shared-state cases run alone under the runner's rules
  end
  CP-->>SW: Case verdicts<br/>full result artifact
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>no missing case is a pass
  %%> Result:
  %%> - case receipts remain in the task copy; no reset follows the final batch, so the author can inspect the resulting state
  %%> - fails_on_base remains case metadata: merge-base replay is not ported to copies (ProofMergeBaseReplay.php)
  alt every required case passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>passed verdicts
    GW-->>AG: Proof passed<br/>continue to stage 4
    %%> Result:
    %%> - record the cases, verdicts and tested checkout for the PR; run affected proofs again after changes
  else a case failed or did not run
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed or unrun cases
    GW--xAG: Fix in the same copy<br/>repeat the affected proof
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no PR opens; a runner gap or infrastructure failure is not evidence that the feature works
  end
